Oscillators -- generation and analysis of oscillator steady states for small graphs
***********************************************************************************

Description
===========

This package supports computations with Kuramoto oscillators, including
computations for the paper [HSS], Harrington, Schenck, Stillman, Algebraic
aspects of homogeneous Kuramoto oscillators (see
https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.16069 ).  For a list of functions, and links to
their documentation nodes, see the end of this page.

Computations from the paper [HSS]
=================================

  * *note Generation of all SCT (simple, connected, 2-connected) graphs on
    small numbers of vertices: Generation of all SCT _lpsimple_cm connected_cm
    2-connected_rp graphs on small numbers of vertices, -- generating all SCT
    graphs on n vertices
  * *note Checking the codimension and irreducible decomposition of the IG
    ideal: Checking the codimension and irreducible decomposition of the IG
    ideal, -- generating all SCT graphs on n vertices
  * *note SCT graphs with exotic solutions: SCT graphs with exotic solutions,
    -- finding graphs of small size with exotic solutions
  * *note Example 4.1_colon_ unique graph on 8 vertices with exotic solutions
    and no induced cycle of length at least 5: Example 4_pd1_co unique graph on
    8 vertices with exotic solutions and no induced cycle of length at least 5,
    -- example 4.1 in arXiv 2312.16069
  * *note Example 4.2_colon_ a K5 and pentagon glued along an edge: Example
    4_pd2_co a K5 and pentagon glued along an edge, -- example 4.2 in arXiv
    2312.16069
  * *note Example 4.3_colon_ examples of gluing two cycles along an edge:
    Example 4_pd3_co examples of gluing two cycles along an edge, -- example
    4.3 in arXiv 2312.16069
  * *note Example 4.4_colon_ The square within a square: Example 4_pd4_co The
    square within a square, -- example 4.4 in arXiv 2312.16069

We show a possible workflow using this package.  We use *note NautyGraphs:
(NautyGraphs)Top, to generate graphs of small size.  We use *note Visualize:
(Visualize)Top, to look at these graphs.

+--------------------------------+
|i1 : needsPackage "Oscillators";|
+--------------------------------+
|i2 : needsPackage "NautyGraphs";|
+--------------------------------+
|i3 : needsPackage "Visualize";  |
+--------------------------------+

