getLinearlyStableSolutions -- Compute linearly stable solutions for the Kuramoto oscillator system associated to a graph
************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        getLinearlyStableSolutions(G)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: (Graphs)Graph,, An undirected, connected graph
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A list of linearly stable solutions
        for the Kuramoto oscillator system associated to the graph

Description
===========

The function getLinearlyStableSolutions computes the linearly stable solutions
for the Kuramoto oscillator system associated to a given graph. The Kuramoto
oscillator system is a system of coupled phase oscillators, where the dynamics
of each oscillator is given by the Kuramoto model. The linear stability of a
solution is determined by the eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix of the system
evaluated at the solution.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({0,1,2,3}, {{0,1},{1,2},{2,3},{0,3}});                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : getLinearlyStableSolutions(G)                                           |
|warning: some solutions are not regular: {5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 13, 14, 15, 16,|
| -- .178229s elapsed                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {{1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0}}                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|17, 18, 19, 20}                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note findRealSolutions: findRealSolutions, -- find real solutions, at
    least one per component for well-conditioned systems
  * *note identifyStability: identifyStability, -- Identify the stability of a
    list of eigenvalues, or of potential solutions to the oscillator system

