isStableSolution -- Check if a given solution is stable for the Kuramoto oscillator system
******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isStableSolution(Jac, sol)
  * Inputs:
      * Jac, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, A matrix representing the
        Jacobian of the Kuramoto oscillator system
      * sol, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A potential solution to the
        Kuramoto oscillator system
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, True if the solution is
        stable, false otherwise

Description
===========

The function isStableSolution checks if a given solution is stable for the
Kuramoto oscillator system. The stability of a solution is determined by the
eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix of the system evaluated at the solution. If
all eigenvalues have negative real parts, the solution is considered stable.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({0,1,2,3}, {{0,1},{1,2},{2,3},{0,3}});       |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = oscRing(G, Reduced => true);                       |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = oscSystem(G, R);                                   |
|                                                            |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                             |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Jac = oscJacobian(G, R);                               |
|                                                            |
|             4      4                                       |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                                        |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : realsols = findRealSolutions I;                        |
|warning: some solutions are not regular: {8, 14, 16, 19, 23}|
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : select(realsols, S -> isStableSolution(Jac, S))        |
|                                                            |
|o6 = {{1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0}}                                   |
|                                                            |
|o6 : List                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note oscJacobian: oscJacobian, -- create the Jacobian for the oscillator
    system associated to a graph
  * *note findRealSolutions: findRealSolutions, -- find real solutions, at
    least one per component for well-conditioned systems
  * *note identifyStability: identifyStability, -- Identify the stability of a
    list of eigenvalues, or of potential solutions to the oscillator system

