oscRing -- create a polynomial ring for a given graph or number of oscillators
******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        S = oscRing G
        S = oscRing n
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The number of oscillators
      * G, a *note graph: (Graphs)Graph,, The number of oscillators is the
        number of vertices in the Graph
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CoefficientRing => a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, default value QQ,
        the coefficient ring to use, for numerical work, *note CC:
        (Macaulay2Doc)CC, is a good choice
      * Symbols => a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, default value
        (x,y), a sequence of two symbols.  The first refers to the cosine of
        the given angles and the second refers to the sine of the given angles
      * Reduced => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, if true, then the angles are reduced to the first angle being 0.
        That is, the number of oscillators will be one less than the number of
        vertices of $G$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 

Description
===========

This function returns a polynomial ring in $2n$ variables representing the
cosine and the sine of $n$ angles. Inputting a number assumes that the vertices
are labeled $0, \ldots, n$.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : oscRing(3, CoefficientRing => CC)                 |
|                                                       |
|o1 = CC  [x ..x , y ..y ]                              |
|       53  0   2   0   2                               |
|                                                       |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : oscRing(3, CoefficientRing => CC, Symbols=>{c, s})|
|                                                       |
|o2 = CC  [c ..c , s ..s ]                              |
|       53  0   2   0   2                               |
|                                                       |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

If one gives a graph with Reduced => true, then the number of angles considered
is one less than the number of vertices of the graph.

+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : G = graph({0,1,2,3}, {{0,1},{1,2},{2,3},{0,3}})   |
|                                                       |
|o3 = Graph{0 => {1, 3}}                                |
|           1 => {0, 2}                                 |
|           2 => {1, 3}                                 |
|           3 => {0, 2}                                 |
|                                                       |
|o3 : Graph                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : oscRing G                                         |
|                                                       |
|o4 = QQ[x ..x , y ..y ]                                |
|         0   3   0   3                                 |
|                                                       |
|o4 : PolynomialRing                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : oscRing(G, CoefficientRing => CC, Reduced => true)|
|                                                       |
|o5 = CC  [x ..x , y ..y ]                              |
|       53  1   3   1   3                               |
|                                                       |
|o5 : PolynomialRing                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------+

