standardSols -- find the "standard solutions" for the oscillator system associated to a graph
*********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        standardSols(G,R)
        standardSols(G)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: (Graphs)Graph,, an undirected, connected graph $G$
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, created with *note oscRing:
        oscRing,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Reduced => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false, if true, then the angles are reduced to the first angle being 0.
        That is, the number of oscillators will be one less than the number of
        vertices of $G$
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a list of the "standard
        solutions" that you get where all the angles are the same. This is the
        same as a certain Segre variety.

Description
===========

The oscillator ideal associated to a graph constructed by *note oscQuadrics:
oscQuadrics, always contains the "standard solutions" as a minimal prime. These
standard solutions are the Segre variety $\mathbb{P}^1\times \mathbb{P}^{n-1}$,
where $n$ is the number of vertices of the graph. These are the solutions where
all the angles are the same.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({0,1,2,3}, {{0,1},{1,2},{2,3},{0,3}});|
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = oscRing(G);                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = oscQuadrics(G, R);                          |
|                                                     |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : any(decompose I, P -> P == standardSols(G, R))  |
|                                                     |
|o4 = true                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note oscRing: oscRing, -- create a polynomial ring for a given graph or
    number of oscillators
  * *note oscSystem: oscSystem, -- the ideal of the reduced equilibrium points
    of a dynamical system of oscillators
  * *note oscJacobian: oscJacobian, -- create the Jacobian for the oscillator
    system associated to a graph

Ways to use standardSols:
=========================

  * "standardSols(Graph)"
  * "standardSols(Graph,Ring)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note standardSols: standardSols, is a *note method function with
options: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

