vertexSpanningPolynomial -- computes the vertex spanning polynomial
*******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        vertexSpanningPolynomial(G)
        vertexSpanningPolynomial(G, R)
  * Inputs:
      * G, a *note graph: (Graphs)Graph,, an undirected, connected graph $G$
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, created with *note oscRing:
        oscRing,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, the vertex
        spanning polynomial of the graph $G$ inside $R$.

Description
===========

Let $S$ be the set of all spanning trees of the graph $G$. For each spanning
tree $T$, let $d_i$ be the degree of $v_i$ in $T$. The vertex spanning
polynomial of a graph $G$ is defined as $\sum_{T\in S} \prod_{v_i \in T}
x_i^{d_i-1}$. The factorization of this polynomial is related to the number of
components of the oscillator ideal of the graph computed via *note oscQuadrics:
oscQuadrics,.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : G = graph({0,1,2,3}, {{0,1},{1,2},{2,3},{0,3}});|
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : vertexSpanningPolynomial G                      |
|                                                     |
|o2 = x x  + x x  + x x  + x x                        |
|      0 1    1 2    0 3    2 3                       |
|                                                     |
|o2 : QQ[x ..x , y ..y ]                              |
|         0   3   0   3                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note oscQuadrics: oscQuadrics, -- find the homogeneous quadrics in the
    homogeneous Kuramoto ideal

Ways to use vertexSpanningPolynomial:
=====================================

  * "vertexSpanningPolynomial(Graph)"
  * "vertexSpanningPolynomial(Graph,Ring)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note vertexSpanningPolynomial: vertexSpanningPolynomial, is a *note
method function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

